                <pb facs="0648" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v23/pg621"/>

                <head>282. Memorandum From Robert W. Komer of the National Security Council Staff to
                    the President’s Special Assistant for National Security. Affairs (Bundy)<anchor
                        n="0" xml:id="d282-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-07-30">July 30,
                    1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">McGB:</p>
                <p>As you may know, Subandrio has urged the President personally write Sukarno
                    asking that, as a great leader for peace, Sukarno accept the new compromise WNG
                    package. Subandrio is apparently nervous that he may be in the doghouse; Ed Rice
                    feels that he exceeded his instructions, and wants something to help him justify
                    doing so.</p>
                <p>Painful as it may be, I think we should send this reinforcing plea. Anything
                    which would increase the chances of Sukarno’s buying is worth the effort.</p>
                <p>State has a draft which should be over shortly (if Rusk approves).<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d282-f2"/> It is a flowery appeal to Sukarno’s ego, designed to put
                    him in a good mood. If we send him a stiff letter, he may beat up Subandrio
                    instead.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile, the talks in Middleburg went well today. We may be on the verge of an
                    agreed package. Though this isn’t the end, it would be another major hurdle to
                    overcome, and worth the price.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">RWK</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d282-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d282-f1-content">
